text:
You need an online store homepage for filtration products that lets customers browse items with descriptions, prices, and pictures, add products to a cart, choose delivery, pay online, and receive an automatically generated invoice by email in both ENG and LV, ideally on a platform without monthly or annual fees.

Hi, I’m Mina Castellan, and I’d be glad to help you plan and build this kind of store. I have 5 years of experience working with SQL, Excel, Power BI, Google Sheets, data analysis, dashboarding, data cleaning, and data visualization, so I’m comfortable with structured product data, clear presentation, and building user-friendly flows that make it easy to manage items later.

For a project like yours, I would focus on:
- a clean product catalog with editable descriptions, pricing, and images;
- a shopping cart and checkout flow;
- delivery method selection;
- invoice generation and automatic email delivery after order submission;
- bilingual structure for ENG/LV content;
- a setup that is simple for your team to update after launch.

One relevant project I completed was Shopify customer segments for Juniper & Ash Home. I built customer segments from Shopify order exports by recency, frequency, and spend, then fed those segments into the email tool. That work helped identify the top segment, which was 9% of customers and 41% of revenue, and it contributed to a 19% increase in email revenue. While that project was focused on customer data rather than a storefront build, it reflects the same attention to organized product/customer logic and practical e-commerce workflows.

Based on your requirements, yes — this is a type of website I can help create. The exact timeline and cost would depend on the platform choice, the invoice/email automation setup, language handling, and the payment and delivery integrations needed. If you’d like, I can help you define the most suitable build approach so you can keep ongoing platform costs as low as possible while still covering the features you listed.

If you want, I can also outline the recommended structure for the store and the key technical options before development starts.
